 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Limit exposure to a single currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or backed by, the same underlying currency (for example several coins quoted in the same stablecoin, or a handful of futures contracts settled in the same currency), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several of your open trades at once.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits the fraction of your [tradable capital](#tradable-balance) that may be committed at the same time to open trades sharing the same underlying (settlement, or for spot pairs, quote) currency - regardless of how many different pairs those trades are in.
+
+When opening (or increasing the size of, via [position adjustments](strategy-callbacks.md#adjust-trade-position)) a trade would push the combined stake committed to its underlying currency above the configured limit, the stake amount for that trade is reduced to fit under the limit - the same way stake amounts are already adjusted to fit `tradable_balance_ratio` or the exchange's max stake limits. If no stake amount above the minimum tradable amount remains, the trade is skipped entirely. This applies identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
+```json
+"max_currency_exposure": 0.5,
+```
+
+With the above configuration, no more than 50% of the tradable capital may be committed at the same time across all open trades that settle in the same currency (e.g. all USDT-margined futures, or all pairs quoted in USDT).
+
+!!! Note
+    This setting is unset (unlimited) by default.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
